      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of losing your self along with him is a deep and devastating kind of grief, and it's a heavy burden to carry. You are not a hollow shell; you are a person who has been profoundly shaped by love, and that love still exists within you, even if it feels muted right now. Starting over doesn't mean building something new from scratch; it can mean simply learning to exist again, one small, quiet moment at a time. Be as gentle with yourself as you would be with a friend in this darkness.",
